            <ArticleTitle>Solitary extra-axial posterior fossa abscess due to neurobrucellosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>710-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neurobrucellosis is a rare manifestation of systemic brucellosis. The incidence of nervous system involvement in chronic Brucellosis is approximately 5%. In this case report a solitary, extra-axial posterior fossa abscess due to neurobrucellosis is presented. The clinical manifestations, diagnosis, and treatment of this unusual condition are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
